    <string name="market_scores_hint">High = signs seen at past cycle highs, low = signs seen at past cycle lows. From 4 points one side dominates, from 7 it is extreme. No price target and no forecast.</string>
    <string name="market_scores_none">No signs of a high or a low are active: a quiet middle phase, the price trend decides.</string>
    <string name="market_scores_info_title">Cycle signals</string>
    <string name="market_scores_info_text">Signs of a possible high count signals seen at past cycle highs: strong overvaluation (MVRV), very high miner revenue (Puell), price far above the 200-day or 200-week average, a parabolic rise and the window 12–18 months after the halving.\n\nSigns of a possible low count signals of past cycle lows: low MVRV, weak miner revenue, a deep drop from the all-time high, price near the 200-week average, falling hashrate and a high more than a year ago.\n\nFrom 4 points with a lead the zone is Bull or Bear, from 7 Extreme. If neither side leads, the price trend decides. 0/10 on both sides means neither euphoria nor capitulation.\n\nNo price target and no forecast: the signals only describe what past cycles looked like.</string>
